== Explanations

#sol-item(1, "A", dense: true, pad: 10pt)[Calculating a percentage transforms data and is processing.]

#sol-item(2, "B", dense: true, pad: 10pt)[The abacus is a manual counting aid.]

#sol-item(3, "D", dense: true, pad: 10pt)[Hollerith's tabulating machines used punched cards for census processing.]

#sol-item(4, "C", dense: true, pad: 10pt)[Vacuum tubes are the conventional first-generation technology.]

#sol-item(5, "B", dense: true, pad: 10pt)[A hybrid system combines analog and digital features.]

#sol-item(6, "D", dense: true, pad: 10pt)[General-purpose refers to varied tasks and digital to discrete data representation.]

#sol-item(7, "C", dense: true, pad: 10pt)[The central processing unit executes instructions.]

#sol-item(8, "D", dense: true, pad: 10pt)[The arithmetic logic unit performs arithmetic and logical operations.]

#sol-item(9, "D", dense: true, pad: 10pt)[The control unit interprets and coordinates operations.]

#sol-item(10, "A", dense: true, pad: 10pt)[A microphone receives sound as input.]

#sol-item(11, "C", dense: true, pad: 10pt)[Optical character recognition recognises characters in images.]

#sol-item(12, "A", dense: true, pad: 10pt)[Optical mark recognition detects marks in predefined positions.]

#sol-item(13, "A", dense: true, pad: 10pt)[A projector displays an enlarged image on a surface.]

#sol-item(14, "B", dense: true, pad: 10pt)[The display is output while detected touches are input.]

#sol-item(15, "C", dense: true, pad: 10pt)[Registers hold immediately needed processor values or addresses.]

#sol-item(16, "C", dense: true, pad: 10pt)[Ordinary RAM is volatile.]

#sol-item(17, "D", dense: true, pad: 10pt)[An HDD uses rotating magnetic platters.]

#sol-item(18, "B", dense: true, pad: 10pt)[Divide 64 bits by eight to obtain eight bytes.]

#sol-item(19, "B", dense: true, pad: 10pt)[Five times 1,024 is 5,120 bytes.]

#sol-item(20, "A", dense: true, pad: 10pt)[The set binary places are sixteen and two, giving eighteen.]

#sol-item(21, "A", dense: true, pad: 10pt)[Decimal six is four plus two, or binary 110.]

#sol-item(22, "B", dense: true, pad: 10pt)[Hexadecimal B represents decimal eleven.]

#sol-item(23, "D", dense: true, pad: 10pt)[There are 200 pixels at one byte each, giving 200 bytes.]

#sol-item(24, "C", dense: true, pad: 10pt)[The operating system manages resources and provides services.]

#sol-item(25, "C", dense: true, pad: 10pt)[A printer driver provides software support for that device.]

#sol-item(26, "D", dense: true, pad: 10pt)[An assembler translates assembly-language instructions.]

#sol-item(27, "B", dense: true, pad: 10pt)[A spreadsheet is designed for organised cell calculations.]

#sol-item(28, "B", dense: true, pad: 10pt)[The relative row reference shifts down by one.]

#sol-item(29, "D", dense: true, pad: 10pt)[The dollar signs fix both the column and row.]

#sol-item(30, "C", dense: true, pad: 10pt)[Moving changes where an item is located.]

#sol-item(31, "C", dense: true, pad: 10pt)[Copy ordinarily leaves the original and creates a second item.]

#sol-item(32, "A", dense: true, pad: 10pt)[A separate recoverable copy of an original is a backup.]

#sol-item(33, "A", dense: true, pad: 10pt)[Clear ventilation helps reduce the likelihood of overheating.]

#sol-item(34, "C", dense: true, pad: 10pt)[A UPS supplies temporary power within its capacity.]

#sol-item(35, "D", dense: true, pad: 10pt)[Electrical hazards should be addressed by qualified personnel.]

#sol-item(36, "D", dense: true, pad: 10pt)[A router forwards traffic between networks.]

#sol-item(37, "B", dense: true, pad: 10pt)[DNS helps resolve domain names to information such as IP addresses.]

#sol-item(38, "A", dense: true, pad: 10pt)[The web is a service that uses the internet.]

#sol-item(39, "A", dense: true, pad: 10pt)[Verify through an independently known channel and do not disclose the password.]

#sol-item(40, "B", dense: true, pad: 10pt)[HTTPS protects communication, not the honesty of the site operator.]
